+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Akvorado requires Kafka and ClickHouse, which are not installed by this
package. Review the Kafka and ClickHouse addresses in
${SYSCONFDIR}/akvorado/akvorado.yaml before starting the services.

The sample configuration runs every service on a single host, each with its
own HTTP port:

    orchestrator  :8080  (configuration served to the other services)
    inlet         :8081  (flows on UDP 2055 NetFlow, 4739 IPFIX, 6343 sFlow)
    outlet        :8082  (BMP on TCP 10179)
    console       :8083  (web interface)

SO_REUSEPORT does not load-balance UDP flows on OpenBSD, so the inlet uses
one worker per listening port.

Start Kafka and ClickHouse first: the orchestrator exits when they are not
reachable, and the other services exit when the orchestrator is not
reachable. Enable the services in this order:

    # rcctl enable akvorado_orchestrator akvorado_inlet akvorado_outlet \
        akvorado_console
    # rcctl start akvorado_orchestrator
    # rcctl start akvorado_inlet akvorado_outlet akvorado_console

GeoIP databases are read from /var/db/GeoIP (see net/geoipupdate).
